.el .ds Aq '
.TH urlmenu-setup 1  "setup " 
.SH NAME
urlmenu\-setup \- Register urlmenu as the default handler for http, https and HTML, and install shell completion. Without a part flag, does both
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBurlmenu setup\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-handler\fR] [\fB\-\-completion\fR] [\fB\-\-undo\fR] [\fB\-\-print\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register urlmenu as the default handler for http, https and HTML, and install shell completion. Without a part flag, does both
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would run as JSON instead of running it
.TP
\fB\-\-handler\fR
Only the default handler: desktop entry and `xdg\-mime default`
.TP
\fB\-\-completion\fR
Only the completion scripts, for each of fish, bash and zsh in `PATH`
.TP
\fB\-\-undo\fR
Remove what setup wrote and restore the previous default handler
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the files and commands instead of applying them
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
